  "summary": "Experience rich savory depth with this crisp <b>Thai flatbread dish</b> centered around complex fermented ingredients. Soft flatbread dough is hand-stretched and cooked on a hot griddle until puffed and golden brown with charred spots. It is served with a fragrant dip made from savory fermented yellow soybean paste, lemongrass, minced garlic, and creamy coconut cream. This fermented paste lends a unique umami core that balances beautifully with sweet palm sugar and fiery red chilies. Fresh Thai basil leaves and chopped roasted peanuts scattered over top provide herbaceous aroma and crunch. The contrasting textures of hot, flaky flatbread paired with warm, pungent soybean dip create an engaging appetizer or light lunch. Rooted in traditional Thai preservation methods, the fermented bean base provides robust flavor without needing hours of preparation. Share this aromatic flatbread platter with friends for an interactive and flavor-packed culinary journey.",
